    "summary_one_sentence": "Facing the dual diagnoses of autism and brittle bone disease in their young son Austin, Scott and Teresa LeRette find unexpected joy and spiritual transformation through their boy's resilient spirit.",
    "summary_short": "When Scott and Teresa LeRette learn their son Austin has both autism and brittle bone disease, their initial fears about his future threaten to overwhelm them. However, Austin's joyous personality and unwavering optimism begin to transform his family's perspective on life's hardships. Guided by Scott's expanding faith and Austin's indestructible positivity, the family learns to embrace every moment with gratitude. Ultimately, they discover that true strength comes not from avoiding life's fractures, but from remaining unbreakable in spirit.",
    "summary_long": "Scott and Teresa LeRette are an ordinary couple facing an extraordinary challenge when their son, Austin, is diagnosed with both autism and osteogenesis imperfecta, commonly known as brittle bone disease. The continuous medical emergencies, hospital visits, and physical limitations initially throw Scott into a deep emotional and spiritual tailspin as he struggles to protect his fragile child. Despite frequent bone fractures and severe physical setbacks, Austin approaches every day with an infectious, boundless enthusiasm that touches everyone around him. Seeing his son's radiant happiness forces Scott to re-examine his own outlook on life, faith, and what it truly means to be strong. As Scott works through his personal struggles and leanings toward faith, Austin becomes a beacon of hope not just for his family, but for his entire community. The film traces the emotional highs and lows of the LeRette family as they learn to navigate complex medical care while building a loving, supportive environment. Through daily acts of courage, Austin demonstrates that physical vulnerability does not dictate a person's capacity for joy. Scott eventually shifts from constant worry to deep gratitude, realizing that Austin's unique way of seeing the world is a profound blessing. By celebrating every small victory together, the LeRette family learns that an indomitable spirit can shatter any hardship.",
    "synopsis": "The Unbreakable Boy tells the inspiring true story of the LeRette family as they navigate the extraordinary journey of raising a child with severe medical conditions. Scott and Teresa LeRette find their world upended when their son Austin is diagnosed with both autism spectrum disorder and brittle bone disease—a rare genetic condition that makes his bones extremely fragile and susceptible to frequent fractures. Initial fear and uncertainty weigh heavily on Scott, who struggles to find meaning and stability amid constant hospital visits and safety precautions. However, Austin defies his physical limitations through an extraordinarily joyful, optimistic demeanor that captivates everyone he meets. Rather than being defined by his diagnoses, Austin lives with open-hearted enthusiasm, teaching those around him to focus on gratitude instead of hardship. As Scott witnesses his son's unbreakable optimism, his own faith and perspective undergo a profound transformation. The narrative explores themes of unconditional love, spiritual growth, resilience, and the deep impact a single positive life can have on an entire community. Warmhearted and deeply emotional, this drama provides an uplifting look at how faith and family can turn life's most fragile moments into a celebration of joy and courage.",
